incident :the_callowhill_duplicate do
  name "The Callowhill Duplicate"
  tags :trade, :identity, :legibility, :governance

  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    In 2089 two people presented the same completion receipt at #{ref :race_street_claim_house, "Race Street Claim House"}, eleven days apart, for the replacement of a chilled-water return riser under a Callowhill Street block. The work had been accepted and priced the previous autumn and the balance stood in #{ref :claim_escrow, "escrow"}. Both presenters gave the buyer, the date and the price, and neither carried an identity record the desk could query without repair.

    #{ref :ruth_osei, "Ruth Osei"} put the same three questions to each: what the line was brought to, how long it was held there, and who was standing at the joints. She had the answers on a certified extract taken off #{ref :the_pressure_schedule, "the Pressure Schedule"} the year before, on a #{ref :the_face_warrant, "warrant"} the claim house had filed for a different riser and a different claim.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :course, heading: "The Two Answers"
    The first presenter put the hold at about a quarter of an hour and called the pressure high, said the gauge was borrowed and read stiff, named the man who walked the line through the hold, and volunteered that two joints above a closed ceiling were signed off without being seen. None of that matches the schedule exactly. All of it is the shape the schedule requires.

    The second presenter gave the price to the cent, the buyer's account reference and the date the offer was posted, and said the line had been tested cold. Asked who watched the joints, they said the building's own crew, who were not on site that week.

    Osei entered the second presentation as not established and kept it on the file rather than destroying it. She then opened the first claimant's identity record, which had split during a #{ref :mercy, "Mercy"} transfer in 2086, and worked it with #{ref :the_receipt_holders, "the Receipt Holders"} until it survived a #{ref :guardianship, "guardian"} query. The balance left reserve under #{ref :the_named_payee_rule, "the Named Payee Rule"}, with the support owed to two registered dependents paid ahead of the claimant.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :aftermath, heading: "Nine Classes Of Plant"
    Nothing happened to the second presenter. Market's rule voids an assignment and provides no offence for offering a receipt at a counter, so the file records a presentation that was not established and a person who left the building.

    The mutual now files a warrant request through #{ref :the_brokers, "the Pearl River houses"} before a claim on plant older than the Breach reaches the identity desk, and the requests queue behind paper the settlements do not make. Osei's run of certified extracts holds nine sheets in #{year :now} CE, covering nine classes of plant, and she will not put the three questions to a claimant on plant she has no extract for.

    At the #{ref :juyan_register_house, "Juyan Register House"} the same case is one line: a face spent, a thickness entered, an album number, and a counterfoil that came back on the western run.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — The examination turns on a witnessed act rather than a remembered figure, which is why the extract is useful even though the surviving edition of the schedule is a modified adoption. The claim house's own limit decided the outcome: a receipt is not a bearer instrument, so establishing which body did the work still leaves the identity record to repair."
end
